simplify is not wired into jsmtlib.properties/the solver adapters yet -- this
script only exists to check jSMTLIB's own error handling when a configured
solver executable can't be found/launched, not simplify itself, but it's
premature to test even that until simplify support actually exists. Also
sidesteps an unresolved Windows-only golden-selection mystery (the .windows
golden with the correct CreateProcess wording isn't being picked up over the
stale bare golden; root cause not pinned down -- see the
jsmtlib_ci_cross_platform_verification memory).
